    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first makes a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into windows without dropping tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into the dense carrier field. The window operator partitions that same field into token windows. The second expression keeps every token by windowing the carrier rather than replacing it.",
